 "about": "Additions to the team's test cases, kept out of meralco_demo.sqlite (that file is never changed): everything here is added to a working copy in memory when the server starts. Delete this file, or set FIRSTLOOK_EXTRA_POLES=off, to run the cases exactly as supplied. Three parts. \"poles\": extra equipment for the 13 supplied cases, so each has ten or eleven things to rank; every row is chosen so that the case's expected answer stays the same. \"cases\": seven more cases written for this build (case-14 to case-20), each with its own expected answer, which must be the answer the database's own rule gives. \"titles\": a plain title for every case, shown on screen instead of the scenario name. backend/tests/test_cases.py checks all of this. Fields left out of a pole take the table's defaults: safety safe, status pending, work_type restore, flood_status clear, no ETA, no distance. \"equipment\" is not a column of the table: it says what kind of equipment the job is on (pole when left out, transformer, or line).",
